# Cloudflare reads this from the build output root.
#
# The JS bundle's filename contains its content hash, so it can be cached
# forever; the HTML must not be, or a deploy leaves people on the old bundle.
#
# Every rule whose path matches applies, in order, and a header two rules both
# set is joined into one comma-separated value — so a hashed bundle matched by
# `/*` and by its own rule would be sent `max-age=0, must-revalidate, public,
# max-age=31536000, immutable`, which a cache may read either way. So `/*`
# comes first with the page defaults, and the specific rules detach its
# Cache-Control (`! Cache-Control`) before setting their own.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/_expo/static/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
